<main class="policy-main"><p class="policy-eyebrow">Your information, in your hands</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="policy-updated">Effective 12 October 2026</p>
<p>This policy explains how ayo.dsgn Life (“Life”, “we”, “us”) handles information when you use the Life planner at life.ayodsgn.com. It covers email and Google sign-in, planner features, optional Google connections, AI assistance, accountability sharing and reminders.</p>
<h2>Information Life uses</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Email accounts:</strong> your email address identifies your Life account. When you choose an email password, Life stores a salted, one-way password hash, never the password itself. Email ownership is not currently verified, and Life never links accounts solely because their email addresses match. For account help, contact the support address below.</li><li><strong>Google sign-in:</strong> your Google account’s stable identifier, name and email address, so Life can authenticate you and keep your planner associated with your account. Google handles your Google password. Life does not receive or store it. Existing owner and invited-partner sign-in uses a separate Life passphrase; Life stores only its one-way password hash.</li><li><strong>Your planner content:</strong> boards, tasks, goals, dates, notes, lists, routines, chat messages, memories, uploaded files and settings you choose to add.</li><li><strong>Optional connections:</strong> if you separately connect Google Calendar or Google Tasks, Life receives the access tokens and the calendar/task data needed to synchronize entries you choose to manage in Life. OAuth refresh tokens are encrypted on Life’s server. You can disconnect Google synchronization in Account &amp; connections; disconnecting removes Life’s stored authorization and does not delete entries already in Google.</li><li><strong>AI requests:</strong> when you use Life’s AI features, the message you submit and relevant planner context are sent from Life’s server to Google Gemini to produce a response or carry out an authorized planner action. Do not include information you do not want processed for that request. The current native voice dock sends microphone audio to Google Gemini in real time; Life saves the conversation transcript, not an audio recording. Typed messages send text.</li><li><strong>Notifications:</strong> if you enable device notifications, Life stores that device’s push subscription and uses it to deliver planner reminders. Reminder text may be handled by the browser or push-delivery provider so it can reach your device.</li><li><strong>Accountability sharing:</strong> if you invite a partner, the planner information and actions shown to that invited person are used to provide the sharing features you enabled.</li><li><strong>Basic service data:</strong> technical request and security information may be processed by Life’s hosting provider to operate and protect the service.</li></ul>
<h2>How we use information</h2><p>Life uses information to provide your private planner, authenticate your account, save and display your content, process AI requests you initiate, perform optional synchronization you authorize, deliver requested reminders, support invited accountability partners, and protect the service. We do not use Google API data for advertising or sell it. Google data is used only to provide or improve the user-facing features you request, consistent with Google’s API Services User Data Policy and Limited Use requirements.</p>
<h2>Where information is processed</h2><p>Planner data is stored by Life’s hosting provider. AI request content is sent to Google Gemini for processing. Google sign-in and any Google Calendar or Tasks access are handled by Google. Push reminders may be routed through the push service used by your browser or device. Those providers process information under their own applicable terms and privacy notices.</p>
<h2>Storage and security</h2><p>Life applies account-level access controls and security measures designed to protect planner content. Google refresh tokens used for optional connections are encrypted on the server. Information is retained while needed to provide the service and maintain your account. To request account or content deletion, email <a href="mailto:iamichaelayomide@gmail.com">iamichaelayomide@gmail.com</a>. We will handle the request and any applicable backup retention through the service’s available deletion process.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2><ul><li>You may use Google sign-in without connecting Calendar or Tasks.</li><li>You can connect Calendar and Tasks separately, and disconnect Google synchronization, in Account &amp; connections.</li><li>You can disable device notifications in your browser or device settings and remove a subscription in Life.</li><li>You can review, change or export planner content from within Life.</li><li>You can request access, correction or deletion by contacting us.</li></ul>
<h2>Children and policy changes</h2><p>Life is intended for people old enough to manage their own planner account and is not designed for children under 13. We may update this policy when the service or its data practices change. We will post the current version here and show the current policy links during sign-in.</p>
<div class="policy-note"><strong>Google password:</strong> Google authenticates your sign-in directly. Life never asks for, sees or stores your Google password.</div>
<p class="policy-footer">Questions or privacy requests: <a href="mailto:iamichaelayomide@gmail.com">iamichaelayomide@gmail.com</a>. See also our <a href="/life/terms.php">Terms of Service</a>.</p></main></body></html>
